    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with high optimism, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.21) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who represent our strongest offensive engines. **Yordan Alvarez** faces Nick Martinez in a matchup where the SP_xERA of 4.72 and his own elite xwOBA of 0.477 suggest a massive ceiling. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-priority play; his dynamic platoon advantage against Andre Pallante, coupled with the stolen base opportunity presented by Pallante\u2019s slow delivery, makes him an essential component of our pursuit of the scarce SB category. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Junior Caminero** (72.33) also provide elite stability, with **Christian Yelich** benefiting significantly from a favorable park factor and a top-of-the-order role that should maximize his counting stat output against the vulnerable Jose Cabrera.\n\nWhile the lineup is optimized for aggressive scoring, we continue to monitor the marginal starts like **Lars Nootbaar** (47.37) and **Caleb Durbin** (45.77), the latter of whom faces a difficult assignment against Reid Detmers. The most contentious decision on the bench involved **Luke Raley**, who fell just short of a starting berth with a score of 38.17. While **Luke Raley** offers a platoon edge, the optimizer favored the higher-floor profiles of our starting outfielders to preserve our daily game caps. We are also tracking **Chase Meidroth** (36.57), who was relegated to the bench not only due to a unfavorable matchup against Gavin Williams but also because of a 38% rain risk that could lead to a shortened outing. With all projected lineups still pending, we remain vigilant regarding potential late-afternoon adjustments that could shift these efficiency scores, especially for lower-slot hitters like **Gary Sanchez**.",
